    "name": "Bookly API",
    "description": "Accounts & auth for Bookly (Express + MongoDB + JWT).\n\nRun **Sign up** (or **Sign in**) first: the test scripts store `accessToken`, `refreshToken` and `userId` in collection variables, and every authenticated request uses `{{accessToken}}` as its Bearer token.\n\nSet `baseUrl` (default http://localhost:4000). Sign up uses a random email each run so the folder can be run top to bottom with the Collection Runner.\n\nErrors always look like `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \"field\" } }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
